{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-71668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨1,-2,5⟩$ and $b=⟨3,-1,-1⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9ef08c4fd09268676b82664916c9763be3840951a84d1e4516266193f35f9c7b"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5"] ["math" "⟨0,0,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}},\\sqrt{5}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{30}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-71668" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,0,0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-212457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨0,1,-5⟩$ and $b=⟨6,x,-2⟩.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-212457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 6+1\\cdot x+(-5)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =x+10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ x+10 & =0 \\\\ x & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-212457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9ef08c4fd09268676b82664916c9763be3840951a84d1e4516266193f35f9c7b"} {"question" "q-212457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-212457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-212457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-212461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-212461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot x \\\\  & =x-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ x-20 & =0 \\\\ x & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-212461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9ef08c4fd09268676b82664916c9763be3840951a84d1e4516266193f35f9c7b"} {"question" "q-212461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-212461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-16"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-212461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $c=⟨2,1,-3⟩$ and $d=⟨4,-2,1⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $c$ onto $d.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c=⟨$  \n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{d}\\,c & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{d\\cdot d}\\,d \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{d}_{x}^{2}+{d}_{y}^{2}+{d}_{z}^{2}}\\,d \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 4+1\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 1}{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\,d \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2-3}{16+4+1}\\,⟨4,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{21}\\,⟨4,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\,⟨4,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{4}{7},-\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{1}{7}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317653" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9ef08c4fd09268676b82664916c9763be3840951a84d1e4516266193f35f9c7b"} {"question" "q-317653" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317653" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317653" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317653" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317653" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317653" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a=⟨$ \n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{6}⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}⟨2,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,5,-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9ef08c4fd09268676b82664916c9763be3840951a84d1e4516266193f35f9c7b"} {"question" "q-317654" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317654" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q-317654" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981143/state.json" "file_sha256" "a3de38f4ba491a33bc80aa902c7c3d88fdbd6ecf4a9d133795051754c06fc30d"} {"question" "q